  "evidence": [
    "Independent pinned-PE and actual application COFF review identifies same-target call boundaries lost by production Ob2 and restored by the private Ob1 control: ten queue-call sites across six Video callers plus member ctor/dtor calls, PullDown UNK1->UNK4->GraphicWin::close, AlphaMovie on_modal->MCIVideo::is_playing and close->MCIVideo::close->GraphicWin::close, and ordered DipEdit treaty/agenda helper calls. Entire112 mapped originals and all current exact controls are in scope, not just six masked gains.",
    "Authorize only source-local Ob1 CMake properties for these four already-built units and corresponding explicit measurement recipes. Preserve DipEdit existing Oy- by appending, never overwriting its source options. Other three retain their existing default frame policy. Preserve global Release flags, linker/runtime/toolchain/build policy, all other unit profiles, sources, headers, object storage, source order, complete original annotations/claims/history and C++ method bodies. No wrappers, noinline attributes, ABI/lifetime rewrites, source moves, deliberate bug fixes or new claims.",
    "Private whole-project Ob1 is diagnostic only and rejected globally:425 old actual exact losses against74 gains. Filemap/Palette apparent gains call wrong new wrappers and are excluded; Path helpers do not select original startup shape and remain excluded. Fresh isolated four-owner build and actual original targets must qualify this batch; do not borrow the global control as production evidence or claim all mismatches disappear.",
    "Review all physical collateral, including Video/AlphaMovie constructors, destructors, member teardown and associated unwind code; DipEdit inherited destructor/unwind contributions; PullDown on_key_click and all neighboring exact controls. Compiler-emitted header contributions require complete code/reference/metadata accounting, never a blanket owner waiver. Keep unknown linked selection/allocation and whole-game/runtime acceptance unknown.",
    "The demonstrated throughput blocker is project tests replaying one-time entire CMake/project snapshots after unrelated owner changes. Authorize only replacing these global snapshot constraints in the three named tests with durable live owner source/profile/global compiler/link policy and damage assertions. Keep full exact task-base/current config delta proof in ignored per-change native audits. Preserve immutable source/body/annotation inverses and synthetic historical parser/damage fixtures. No blanket xfail, deleting useful controls, baseline reset, default weakening or unrelated zlib test edits; report baseline failures separately.",
    "Coordinator alone owns Git/compiler leases/integration. Tests workers edit disjoint assigned paths and freeze before measurements. Require fresh full build/link, all112 subjects measured together per required source context, all exact controls preserved, original direct-target/ordered multiplicity/lifetime checks, native whole-application outside-scope observations, independent actual source/physical review, claims/mappings/references and destination rechecks before cleanup. Manual integration does not assert original historical TUs, full native acceptance or a working game."
  ],
  "intent": "Restore original out-of-line call and member-lifetime boundaries across the complete Video, PullDown, AlphaMovie and DipEdit owners using their evidence-backed per-unit automatic-inlining policy.",
